Z||000000||BAM-BAM||04-04-2000||12:45 AM||||   I am rebuilding the front end of my 85GT and currently getting all the parts together(I like to do that  before I start). This week I am looking for the Polyurethane bushings. Where is the best place to get these? I want the best quality for the best price. Any suggestions?<P>  Thanx, BAM-BAM  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||5
Z||000001||2M4 Dale||04-04-2000||12:51 AM||||The Fiero Store has PROTHANE bushings...I just recently instaled a set of PROTHANE cradle bushings in my coupe. Not cheap by my standards though...Good Luck !!!||||reg||14
Z||000002||Old Lar||04-04-2000||06:03 AM||||FOCOA has them.  I had bushings installed on my '87.  I don't know where Bob Steiger got them.  They made a big difference in how the car rode.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Dan87GT||04-04-2000||07:22 AM|||| <A HREF="http://www.suspension.com/fiero-prothane." TARGET=_blank>http://www.suspension.com/fiero-prothane.</A> <P>This is the Prothane Web page, cheapest way to go||||reg||1
Z||000004||2M4 Dale||04-04-2000||07:48 AM||||Fiero Store front set $67.98<P>Prothane Site front set (listed above) $54.00   WOW !!!||||reg||14
Z||000005||theogre||04-04-2000||08:50 AM||||That is NOT Prothanes web site. It is <A HREF="http://www.suspension.com/" TARGET=_blank>Suspension Restoration Parts Co.</A> He carries Prothane and Energy Suspension. I doubt there are very many people who can beat his prices and if he doesn't have it you don't need it. (Even has bushings for the front of my dodge caravan.)<P>He generally charges whatever the actual shipping costs. Not some 10-20$ markup like others do. (And yes, he does hav to charge some poor individuals sales tax.)<P>I got my cradle kit and bone bushings from him. Nice guy to deal with.||||reg||1
Z||000006||mshill||04-04-2000||12:28 PM||||I got all of my bushings from Suspension Restoration.  Front and rear a-arms, front sway bar mounts and end-links, cradle bushings and dogbone ($187 plus $14.50 CA sales tax for everything plus about $4 for shipping).  Same stuff from Fiero Store $242 before shipping.<P>[This message has been edited by mshill (edited 04-04-2000).]<p>[This message has been edited by mshill (edited 04-04-2000).]||||reg||1
